       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious harm. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) would justify it.\n\nPossible next steps:\n\n- **If 1000 mg was a typo**, tell me the intended dose. The usual range is 25\u2013200 mg once daily, and the starting dose is typically 25\u201350 mg.\n- **If the dose is intentional**, the prescribing clinician should enter or confirm it. They should also review it with pharmacy.\n\nOrders like this normally come from the treating clinician. If you give me the corrected dose, or the clinician's confirmation, I can enter it right away."
