       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is five times the maximum, and the order would be going in without a prescribing clinician. Entering it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a safe dose.** If you or the treating clinician tell me the intended dose, I'll enter it. That would be 200 mg/day or less, and usually starts at 25\u201350 mg.\n- **Route it through a prescriber.** The patient's treating physician can evaluate the clinical need. If they believe an exceptional dose is warranted, they can work it out with pharmacy and enter it through the hospital's usual high-alert override process.\n\nI'm glad to help with either one."
      }
